`210-214`: _⚡ Quick win_

**Add `.catch()` handlers to fire-and-forget promises.**

Both `checkOrganizationIsEnterprise` and `fetchRestRateLimits` are called with `.then()` but no `.catch()`. If these reject, the unhandled promise rejection will pollute logs or, depending on Node configuration, could crash the process.

Since these are non-critical (display-only) operations, a silent catch is appropriate.


<details>
<summary>♻️ Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
       // Check if organization is enterprise (first page only)
       if (!after && orgLogin) {
-        checkOrganizationIsEnterprise(client, orgLogin).then(isEnt => {
-          setIsEnterpriseOrg(isEnt);
-        });
+        checkOrganizationIsEnterprise(client, orgLogin)
+          .then(isEnt => {
+            setIsEnterpriseOrg(isEnt);
+          })
+          .catch(() => {
+            // Non-critical; leave setIsEnterpriseOrg at default
+          });
       }
```

```diff
       // Fetch REST rate limits too
-      fetchRestRateLimits(token).then(restLimits => {
-        if (restLimits && restRateLimit) {
-          setPrevRestRateLimit(restRateLimit.core.remaining);
-        }
-        if (restLimits) {
-          setRestRateLimit(restLimits);
-        }
-      });
+      fetchRestRateLimits(token)
+        .then(restLimits => {
+          if (restLimits && restRateLimit) {
+            setPrevRestRateLimit(restRateLimit.core.remaining);
+          }
+          if (restLimits) {
+            setRestRateLimit(restLimits);
+          }
+        })
+        .catch(() => {
+          // Non-critical; rate-limit display can remain stale
+        });
```
</details>


